surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Baron</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pecorelli</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Randomized Intergroup trial of cisplatin-paclitaxel versus cisplatin-cyclophosphamide in women with advanced epithelial ovarian cancer: 3 year results</article-title><source>J Nat Cancer Inst</source><year>2000</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>699</fpage><lpage>708</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Nat Cancer Inst||92|699||bib2|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib3"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vasey</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaye</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Thigpen</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of dose-intensity in ovarian cancer</article-title><source>Ovarian Cancer, Controversies in Management</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>New York: Churchill Livingstone</publisher-name><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>168</lpage>Gershenson D and McGuire WP (eds)</citation></ref><ref id="bib4"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wahl</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Fairchild</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>FY</given-names></name><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Demers</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Galloway</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Loss of normal p53 function confers sensitization to Taxol</article-title><source>Nature Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Nature Med||2|72||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="p